Analysis of jitdump (AI generated)

## Analysis (AI generated)

Assertion: `!m_dfsTree->Contains(HBtab->ebdFilter)` — `fgehopt.cpp:1900` in `fgRemoveUnreachableTry`.

The method has a deeply nested EH layout: outer `try/filter-catch` (EH#3), an inner `try/catch` (EH#2), whose catch holds a `try/finally` (EH#0) wrapped in a `try/filter-catch` (EH#1). After earlier opts (the `return` makes the inner regions dead), EH#1 is `try BB17..BB19 / filter BB21..BB24 / handler BB25`.

The phase finds EH#1's try entry BB17 unreachable and asserts the documented invariant: an unreachable try implies an unreachable filter. Here that fails — BB21 (the filter) is still in the DFS tree. The header comment notes the EH-aware DFS _normally_ makes try-reachability imply filter-reachability, but with two-pass EH dispatch from an outer filter, a filter can remain DFS-reachable while its try is not, so the `assert` fires.

Root cause: `fgRemoveUnreachableTry` assumes a filter is unreachable whenever its try is unreachable, but nested two-pass filter dispatch can keep the filter live. The phase needs to handle dead-try-with-live-filter rather than asserting. Same family as the other `Remove unreachable try` assertions (`ebdHndLast`/`ebdTryBeg` verifier failures, residual `bbRefs`).

Attached details.zip file that includes the repro.mc and jitdump.txt files for this example.

